  "content": {
    "id": "p14-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "The space diagonal of a rectangular prism is 1 cm longer than its first side, 5 cm longer than its second side, and 8 cm longer than its third side. Find the length of the space diagonal.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$9\\text{ cm}$.\n\nSubstitute the sides $d-1$, $d-5$ and $d-8$ into the space-diagonal formula; require $d>8$.",
      "worked": "Let $d$ cm be the space diagonal. The sides are $(d-1)$ cm, $(d-5)$ cm and $(d-8)$ cm.\n$$\\begin{align*}d^2&=(d-1)^2+(d-5)^2+(d-8)^2\\\\d^2&=3d^2-28d+90\\\\0&=2d^2-28d+90\\\\0&=d^2-14d+45\\\\0&=(d-5)(d-9)\\\\d&=5\\text{ or }9.\\end{align*}$$\nAll side lengths must be positive, so $d>8$. Therefore the space diagonal is $9\\text{ cm}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 68
  },
